    "type": "question",
    "label": "9",
    "prompt": "Differentiate $e^{\\tan x}$, and hence find $\\displaystyle\\int_0^{\\pi/4}\\sec^2x\\,e^{\\tan x}\\,dx$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\dfrac{d}{dx}e^{\\tan x}=\\sec^2x\\,e^{\\tan x}$; integral $=e-1$.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{d}{dx}e^{\\tan x}&=\\sec^2x\\,e^{\\tan x}.\\end{align*}$$\nHence\n$$\\begin{align*}\\int_0^{\\pi/4}\\sec^2x\\,e^{\\tan x}\\,dx&=\\left[e^{\\tan x}\\right]_0^{\\pi/4}\\\\&=e^{\\tan(\\pi/4)}-e^{\\tan 0}\\\\&=e^1-e^0\\\\&=e-1.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 33
  },
